  "method": "Centre from a least-squares circle fit to OpenStreetMap way(s) tagged 'Outer Ring Road' (20 way segments, 173 vertices total, fit centre 41.831724,-88.251594, fitted radius 973.7 m, rms 57.2 m -- reproducing the integrator's independent fit exactly). Radius is set from the sourced circumference (Shiltsev 2011: 'circumference of 6.3 km' -> 6300/(2*pi) = 1002.68 m) rather than the ring-road's own fitted radius, since the road is an inner service loop. Cross-checked (see checks[]) against the OSM-sourced CDF (B0) and D0 collision-hall building centroids: both sit within 1.2% of the sourced radius from this same centre (1003.9 m and 990.8 m respectively), and their great-circle separation (1768.9 m) subtends about 124.6 degrees at this centre, close to the '1/3 of the ring apart' relationship between B0 and D0 -- strong independent corroboration that the fitted centre and sourced radius describe a real circular ring, even though no single fetched source explicitly uses the word 'circular'. Haversine on R=6371008.8 m.",
